- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** Stage one fits each AIR trace by two cosine coefficients (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:freeCosineFit`; the LP-frame fit of step 349 read through `MuellerReconstruction.fs:sourceCplFromLpFrame`), but a calibration's results are wanted in the instruments' own constants, the values step 389 writes, so that each gets its σ, correlation and profile like any other fitted parameter (001 §L 'value ± σ'; S11.5 publishes each calibrated value with its σ, 001 §I). The same two cosine models are written here in those constants: a reparameterisation that is one-to-one on the physical branch, so each fit's minimum and residual are unchanged and FitQuality's covariance in the constants is the propagated one, with no second formula for it. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349, 388): (1) `reduceAirTraces` (step 349; its AIR-label filter gone since step 388) becomes public, its body unchanged: the AIR trace of capture rows, averaged per dial reading, dark-subtracted and normalised per experiment label, which stage one fits and S11.4's per-run residuals read. (2) After it, `type AirTrace with member this.fringeResidualAt (zero : Angle) (visibility : FringeVisibility) : ResidualVector` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AirTrace`, `:FringeVisibility`): entry i is V · cos 2(αᵢ − z) − (normᵢ − 1), αᵢ the trace's dial angle read in degrees as `freeCosineFit` reads it. This is `freeCosineFit`'s model p · cos 2α + q · sin 2α − (norm − 1) at the zero and visibility it reports, p = V cos 2z and q = V sin 2z. (3) `type SourceCplModel with member this.lpFrameResidualOn (trace : AirTrace) (lpZero : Angle) : ResidualVector` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:SourceCplModel`): entry i is q_LP · cos 2(αᵢ − z_LP) + u_LP · sin 2(αᵢ − z_LP) − (normᵢ − 1), the LP-frame fit's model phased on `lpZero`, with 1 − q_LP = (1 − cos δ) · sin² 2θ and u_LP = (1 − cos δ) · sin 2θ · cos 2θ for θ its `thetaRel` and δ its `retardance`. These are the coefficients `sourceCplFromLpFrame` reads back as this model wherever 0° < θ < 90°, its physical branch (its doc: '2θ = atan2(1 − qLp, uLp)', 'cosδ = 1 − (1 − qLp) / sin²2θ'); the doc names the branch. No other declaration changes. Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over test-local `AirTrace`s at the dial angles 0° to 160° by 20°: `an AIR trace's fringe residual at its cosine fit's zero and visibility is that fit's residual`: with normᵢ − 1 = 0.54 · cos 2αᵢ − 0.62 · sin 2αᵢ + 0.01 · (−1)ⁱ, `freeCosineFit (createMathNetSvd ())` answers a zero and a visibility whose `fringeResidualAt` equals, entry by entry within 1e-12, the fit's design times its coefficients less (norm − 1), the coefficients recomputed in the test as V cos 2z and V sin 2z, and whose root mean square is the fit's `rmse` within 1e-12; `an LP-frame residual vanishes on the trace of the source model sourceCplFromLpFrame reads`: with normᵢ − 1 = 0.16 · cos 2(αᵢ − 155°) + 0.17 · sin 2(αᵢ − 155°), `(sourceCplFromLpFrame (CosineCoefficient 0.16) (CosineCoefficient 0.17)).lpFrameResidualOn trace (Angle.degree 155.0<deg>)` is zero within 1e-12 in every entry; `the AIR trace of two experiments' rows is each experiment's trace in turn`: `reduceAirTraces` of two experiments' AIR rows is the trace of the first experiment's rows followed by the second's, angle for angle and value for value. `MuellerReconstructionTests` runs unchanged, every number bit-identical.

**Acceptance.** After the fringes land, `reduceAirTraces` MUST be public and unchanged, `AirTrace.fringeResidualAt` MUST be the free cosine fit's residual in the zero and visibility it reports, and `SourceCplModel.lpFrameResidualOn` the LP-frame fit's residual in the source model it reads back; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an AIR trace's fringe residual at its cosine fit's zero and visibility is that fit's residual`, `an LP-frame residual vanishes on the trace of the source model sourceCplFromLpFrame reads` and `the AIR trace of two experiments' rows is each experiment's trace in turn`, the count rising by 3; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` with every number unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s39 invariants MUST pass.
